196	This is inlined here as it is on the fast path for allocation functions.
197	We have 4 models:
198	
199	- MI_TLS_MODEL_LOCAL: use regular thread local (default on Linux, FreeBSD, etc)
200	    On most platforms (Linux, FreeBSD, NetBSD, etc), this just returns a
201	    thread local variable (`__mi_theap_default`). With the initial-exec TLS model this ensures
202	    that the storage will always be available and properly initialized (with an empty theap).
203	
204	    On some platforms the underlying TLS implementation (or the loader) will call itself `malloc`
205	    on a first access to a thread local and recurse in the MI_TLS_MODEL_LOCAL.
206	    A way around this is to define MI_TLS_RECURSE_GUARD which adds an extra check if the process
207	    is initialized before accessing the thread-local. This is a check in the fast path though
208	    so this should be avoided.
209	
210	- MI_TLS_MODEL_PTHREADS: use `pthread_getspecific`. (default on macOS and OpenBSD, maybe good for Android as well?)
211	    Use pthread local storage. Can be as fast as thread locals on many platforms (like recent macOS).
