213	- MI_TLS_MODEL_FIXED: use a fixed slot in the TLS block.
214	    This reserves an unused and fixed TLS slot. This is fast and avoids the problem
215	    where the underlying TLS implementation (or the loader) will call itself `malloc`
216	    on a first access to a thread local (and recurse in the MI_TLS_MODEL_LOCAL).
217	    This goes wrong though if the OS or a library uses the same fixed slot, and also
218	    prevents multiple instances of mimalloc in the same process.
